    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (263 tests, 0 failures). Here's a summary of what I changed.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key per the spec:\n\n**`identityKey` = SHA-256 hex over `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)`**\n\n### New shared utility\n- **`util/OwnerIdentity.java`** \u2014 a single source of truth holding `identityKey(telephone, email, lastName)`, `sha256Hex(...)`, and a standard American `soundex(...)`. This is used by both the controller (for detection) and the mapper (for the response field), so they agree exactly. (I extracted it here because default methods on the MapStruct-mapped interface were picked up as ambiguous String\u2192String mapping candidates.)\n\n### `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`\n- **Duplicate detection (409)** now compares the single new identity key against existing non-deleted owners. The email-domain blocklist check still runs first (unchanged), and deleted owners are still ignored. The `householdId` no longer participates in duplicate detection (it's still computed/stored and used for household-size/membership features).\n- **Soft match** now sets `possibleDuplicateOf` when an existing non-deleted owner shares this owner's **postcode** and **`soundex(lastName)`** but has a **different identity key** (e.g. a different telephone) \u2014 replacing the previous \"always null\" behavior.\n- Existing owners' telephones are normalized via `toE164(...)` before keying, matching the spec's \"normalizedTelephone.\"\n\n### `OwnerMapper.formatIdentityKey`\n- Now returns the full 64-char lower-case SHA-256 hex via `OwnerIdentity`, so the response's `identityKey` is the redesigned key.\n\n### Docs / tests\n- Updated the `openapi.yml` `identityKey` description to the new algorithm.\n- Updated `OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.createOwnerDuplicateTelephoneReturnsConflict`: it previously asserted the *old* behavior (same telephone \u2192 409 regardless of surname). Under the new spec, \"Doe\" vs \"Roe\" have different soundex codes and are correctly no longer a hard duplicate \u2014 this is precisely the behavior change the spec mandates. I gave both owners the same surname so the test still verifies its actual intent (a differently-formatted telephone normalizing to the same digits, for the same identity, is rejected) under the new key.\n\n**Behavior change now in effect:** two owners with the same last name and postcode but *different telephones* are no longer a hard 409 \u2014 they're created, with the second flagged as a soft match (`possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`).\n\nNote: one pre-existing test (`createOwnerDuplicateTelephoneReturnsConflict`) directly encoded the superseded behavior, so I updated it to match the new specification rather than the old one. Flagging that explicitly since it's the one existing test I had to touch.",
